# The three places a translation counts something once that the model mentions twice. One row per
# elimination: the sum before, the overlap, and what names the overlap.
#
# Each is inclusion-exclusion with a derived correction
#   `x = Σ parts − e`, and `e` is a filed number nowhere here: the overlap of two lane sets is the
#   layer set, the overlap of many part references is the document, and the overlap of three
#   buffers is the layer they are substitutes within. Each is a relation with a name, which is
#   exactly the test that made `eliminations/derived.sqlc` possible. A translation that could not
#   name its overlap would have to file one, and nothing in BPMN could hold it.
#
# The first is the model's, not the emitter's
#   It is the one worth knowing. `pm.draw` has no `buffer` column, so a draw is against a layer and
#   never against one of its three engines. The model already made that elimination, on the ground
#   that the buffers are substitutes (`layers/absorption.sqlc`), and every diagram inherits it.
#   The engine missing from D's key is the elimination.
#
# A fourth collapse would be unsound
#   That is why it is not on this list. Dropping a part's lane membership would count each call
#   once instead of once as a node and once as a placement, but the overlap there is not
#   derivable: a call outside a lane has lost which layer it feeds, so what remains says only that
#   there is nesting here, which is what a subProcess already is. That is an elimination of F's
#   head, and `diagrams/lane_membership.sqlc` refuses it.
-- the derived overlaps a BPMN emission takes, each against the relation that names it.
SELECT * FROM (VALUES
  ('the buffer',   'D would be P x L x 3',        'the layer, within which the three engines are substitutes',
                   'layers/absorption.sqlc'),
  ('the lane set', 'D lanes + N lanes',            'the layer set, enumerated twice over one conformed dimension',
                   'diagrams/lane_grain.sqlc'),
  ('the import',   'one per cross-document part',  'the document, referenced many times from one filing',
                   'diagrams/cross_document.sqlc')
) AS e(elimination, the_sum, the_overlap, named_by)
